    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d525">

                <pb facs="0587" n="471" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg471"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/1165.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-05-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 5, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Foreign Office has just forwarded to this Legation a copy of a decree dated April
                    29, declaring a blockade against Fort Liberté and Cape Haitien. At present it is
                    not effective as both <hi rendition="#italic">Pacifique</hi> and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Nord Alexis</hi> were here until this morning when they
                    sailed carrying troops; destination supposed to be Gonaives.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
